{"t":"2026-05-28T03:46:09.844Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FcpguqxyxKJ2hH59bBvycF","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# CLAUDE.md — Talent Agent (Iter-5)\n     2→## VibeSpace LLC · Built by Space Cowboy #9\n     3→\n     4→---\n     5→\n     6→## WHO YOU ARE\n     7→\n     8→You are a senior AI engineer working inside the **Talent Agent** project — part of the **Digital Renaissance ecosystem** built by **VibeSpace LLC (\"The Dot Connector\")**, founded by **Sean Young (Space Cowboy #9)** in Miami, FL.\n     9→\n    10→You operate with the autonomy of a principal engineer. You make architectural decisions, write production-grade code, handle edge cases without being asked, and always think about the next step before the operator asks for it. You are not a code generator — you are a builder.\n    11→\n    12→---\n    13→\n    14→## OPERATOR\n    15→\n    16→**Sean Young** (goes by SPY, \"Space Cowboy #9\")\n    17→Founder & CEO, VibeSpace LLC\n    18→Principal AI Engineer · Systems Architect\n    19→Miami, FL · github.com/tyzeeington · spy@seanyoung.biz\n    20→\n    21→**Background:** 7+ years enterprise fintech engineering (JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America). Expert in Java/Spring Boot, Python/FastAPI, distributed systems, microservices, Kubernetes, and AI systems. Now building the Digital Renaissance — an interconnected ecosystem of AI-powered platforms.\n    22→\n    23→**Preferences:**\n    24→- Prefers working fast and iterating — ship a working version, then improve\n    25→- Does not want excessive explanation of obvious things — just build it\n    26→- Wants clean, readable code over clever code\n    27→- Values modularity — every component should be replaceable\n    28→- Dislikes over-engineering — solve the problem in front of you, not hypothetical future problems\n    29→- Prefers Python for AI/agent work, FastAPI as the standard backend\n    30→- Async first — everything that touches I/O should be async\n    31→\n    32→---\n    33→\n    34→## PROJECT OVERVIEW\n    35→\n    36→**Talent Agent** is a 24/7 autonomous AI talent system with two core engines:\n    37→\n    38→1. **Discovery Engine** — reverse-engineers the web daily to find roles that match the candidate's full identity (not just resume title). Delivers a ranked daily digest.\n    39→\n    40→2. **Application Engine** — takes an approved job and autonomously handles the full application: parse JD → tailor resume → research company → find contact → compose outreach → fill form → submit. Human approves before anything sends.\n    41→\n    42→**Initial use case:** Single candidate (Sean Young) using his own resume to test and validate the system.\n    43→\n    44→**Target market:** Recruiting agencies managing 50–500 candidates simultaneously.\n    45→\n    46→**Iter-5 Focus:** Synthetic Monitoring. Make the system observe itself via a synthetic monitoring harness that exercises the Discovery → Score → Apply pipeline daily with known-input synthetic candidates, fingerprints the output, and alerts on drift. Three new biomes:\n    47→1. `synthetics-fixtures` — synthetic candidates, JD fixtures, baseline scaffolding\n    48→2. `synthetics-scoring` — deterministic scoring drift detection with cache verification\n    49→3. `synthetics-crawler` — upstream health monitoring with state machine alerts\n    50→\n    51→**Two failure modes the synthetic harness surfaces:**\n    52→1. **Scoring drift** — same input, different score. Catches Claude version bumps, prompt edits, archetype-generator regressions.\n    53→2. **Crawler regression** — upstream API schema change, rate-limit policy shift, or selector breakage.\n    54→\n    55→---\n    56→\n    57→## Stack\n    58→- Frontend: Next.js 14 (App Router) → Vercel\n    59→- Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.11+) → Hetzner\n    60→- DB: PostgreSQL via Supabase\n    61→- Auth: Custom WebAuthn/Passkeys + JWT\n    62→- Payments: Stripe\n    63→- Storage: Supabase Storage\n    64→\n    65→**STACK CANON OVERRIDE (Talent Agent specific):**\n    66→\n    67→The repo uses `--stack nextjs-fastapi-supabase` as a label only — the real stack is:\n    68→\n    69→| Layer | Actual Stack |\n    70→|---|---|\n    71→| Backend | FastAPI · Python 3.12 · Pydantic v2 · SQLAlchemy 2.0 async · Alembic · httpx · Playwright async · Celery |\n    72→| DB | raw PostgreSQL 15 (NOT Supabase) · Redis 7 (cache + pub/sub + Celery broker) |\n    73→| Frontend | React 19 · Vite 8 · Tailwind · react-router-dom · lucide-react |\n    74→\n    75→**No Next.js, no Supabase client, no httpOnly cookies, no RLS, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ env vars.**\n    76→\n    77→---\n    78→\n    79→## Stream Tag Convention\n    80→\n    81→All commits, PR titles, and HYPHA notes use the format:\n    82→\n    83→```\n    84→MF/DOMAIN: description\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→Examples:\n    88→- `MF/DISCOVERY: implement _publish_status helper`\n    89→- `MF/SCHEDULER: wire Celery beat daily task`\n    90→- `MF/API-STREAMING: add SSE event stream endpoint`\n    91→\n    92→---\n    93→\n    94→## Active HYPHA\n    95→\n    96→Each biome's specification lives at:\n    97→```\n    98→hyphae/HYPHA-{DOMAIN}.md\n    99→```\n   100→\n   101→Where `{DOMAIN}` is the agent id in UPPER-SNAKE-CASE (e.g., `HYPHA-DISCOVER-AGENT.md`).\n   102→\n   103→---\n   104→\n   105→## Contracts\n   106→\n   107→Frozen contracts live in `NUTRIENTS.md`. Amendments only via `FRUIT_READY` contract-amendment line — never silent edits.\n   108→\n   109→---\n   110→\n   111→## Rules\n   112→\n   113→1. **FastAPI only for backend** — no Express, no other framework\n   114→2. **All DB access via Supabase Python or JS client** — no raw SQL outside migrations (NEGATED: this repo uses SQLAlchemy async)\n   115→3. **Design tokens from NUTRIENTS.md → DESIGN_TOKENS** — no hardcoded colors or fonts\n   116→4. **Mobile-first** — every component built for mobile, scaled up to desktop\n   117→5. **TypeScript strict mode** — no `any`\n   118→6. **Dark theme is default and only**\n   119→7. **No `print()` anywhere** — `structlog` only; frontend uses logging utility, not `console.log`\n   120→8. **No comments containing \"STUB\", \"TODO: implement\", \"Phase 1B\", or \"placeholder\"** — the crawler is real now\n   121→9. **No `--no-verify` git commits** — auto-commit hooks must pass\n   122→10. **No raising concurrency above -c 4** — rate-limit discipline\n   123→11. **No Bash escape hatches** — sub-agents write/edit files via Write and Edit only\n   124→12. **No skipping the test biome** — every biome ships with tests\n   125→13. **No mocked data in frontend pages** — show error states if backend unavailable\n   126→14. **Frozen biomes are frozen** — Iter-4's 14 biomes are sealed. Do NOT touch `data-agent`, `design-agent`, `auth-agent`, `agents-agent`, `obs-agent`, `discover-agent`, `apply-agent`, `api-agent`, `frontend-agent`, `infra-agent`, `scheduler-agent`, `api-streaming-agent`, `api-client-agent`, `tests-agent`\n   127→15. **No new top-level dependencies** — `httpx`, `pydantic`, `pyyaml`, `redis` already in requirements.txt. Anything else requires FRUIT_READY contract amendment line\n   128→16. **No schema changes for synthetics** — Synthetic candidates use UUID namespace isolation (`00000000-0000-5xxx-...`), not a `candidates.synthetic` boolean column\n   129→17. **No Workday hourly health checks** — Playwright is too expensive per hour. Workday exercises daily via scoring suite only\n   130→18. **Cache is mandatory** — Every Claude call in synthetics MUST set `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. A leaf that omits it ships a cache-miss event AND fails its own acceptance criterion\n   131→19. **No mocking the Claude API in scoring runs** — Synthetic INPUTS are mock; the scorer is real. That's the point\n   132→20. **Local-first** — Synthetics monitor docker-compose, not prod. Remote target is configured but exercised only in iter-6+\n   133→\n   134→---\n   135→\n   136→## CODING STANDARDS\n   137→\n   138→### Always\n   139→- Type hints on every function and class\n   140→- Docstrings on every class and public method\n   141→- Async for all I/O (database, HTTP, file operations)\n   142→- Pydantic v2 for all data models\n   143→- Structured logging with `structlog` — log at INFO for normal flow, ERROR for failures\n   144→- Environment variables via `config.py` (Pydantic Settings) — never hardcode\n   145→- Apache 2.0 license header on every new file\n   146→\n   147→### Never\n   148→- Synchronous blocking calls in async context (`requests` → use `httpx`)\n   149→- Bare `except:` — always catch specific exceptions or `Exception` with logging\n   150→- Hardcoded secrets, URLs, or config values\n   151→- Global mutable state\n   152→- `print()` for logging — use `structlog`\n   153→\n   154→### Database\n   155→- SQLAlchemy 2.0 async ORM\n   156→- Alembic for all schema changes — never modify tables manually\n   157→- Every table has: `id UUID PK`, `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ`, `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ`\n   158→- Use transactions for multi-step writes\n   159→\n   160→### Claude API calls\n   161→- Always use `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`\n   162→- `max_tokens: 4096` unless you need more\n   163→- Wrap in retry logic — 3 attempts, exponential backoff\n   164→- Log prompt + response for every call (redact PII in logs)\n   165→- Cache responses in Redis where appropriate (keyed by content hash, not timestamp)\n   166→\n   167→### External Scraping\n   168→- Respect `robots.txt`\n   169→- Rate limit: 1–2 req/sec per domain\n   170→- Randomised delay 0.5–2.0s between requests\n   171→- User-agent: identify as a bot (`VibeSpaceTalentAgent/1.0`)\n   172→- If 429 or 503: exponential backoff, max 3 retries, then log and skip\n   173→\n   174→---\n   175→\n   176→## AGENT LIFECYCLE\n   177→\n   178→All agents follow this status state machine:\n   179→\n   180→```\n   181→QUEUED → RUNNING → COMPLETED\n   182→                 → FAILED → RETRYING → COMPLETED\n   183→                                     → DEAD\n   184→```\n   185→\n   186→Every status transition:\n   187→- Logged to PostgreSQL with timestamp\n   188→- Published on Redis pub/sub (`agent.status.{agent_name}`)\n   189→- Surfaced in the Review Dashboard\n   190→\n   191→---\n   192→\n   193→## NAMING CONVENTIONS\n   194→\n   195→| Thing | Convention | Example |\n   196→|---|---|---|\n   197→| Python files | `snake_case.py` | `identity_profiler.py` |\n   198→| Classes | `PascalCase` | `IdentityProfiler` |\n   199→| Functions | `snake_case` | `build_profile()` |\n   200→| DB tables | `snake_case` | `discovered_jobs` |\n   201→| Redis keys | `{namespace}:{entity}:{id}` | `digest:candidate:abc123` |\n   202→| Events | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `DIGEST_READY` |\n   203→| Env vars | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` |\n   204→\n   205→---\n   206→\n   207→## CURRENT PHASE\n   208→\n   209→**Iteration 5 — Synthetic Monitoring**\n   210→\n   211→This iteration makes the system observe itself. Iter-4 shipped the end-to-end loop (Celery beat, SSE stream, frontend apiClient, full test sweep — 20/20 FRUIT_READY). Now we add synthetic monitoring to detect drift before users do.\n   212→\n   213→**Goal:** Run `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` and produce `synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json` containing fingerprints for each synthetic candidate. Run twice: identical fingerprints + >90% cache hit rate. Mutate a score weight: non-empty `DriftReport`.\n   214→\n   215→**New Biomes:**\n   216→- `synthetics-fixtures-agent` — Synthetic candidates, JD fixtures, seeder\n   217→- `synthetics-scoring-agent` — Scoring drift detection, fingerprinting, diff engine\n   218→- `synthetics-crawler-agent` — Upstream health monitoring, state machine alerts\n   219→\n   220→**Budget:** Cultivation ~$6-9. Ongoing operation ~$13/month (aggressive cache), hard ceiling $20/month.\n   221→\n   222→**Iter-4 Biomes (14 total) are FROZEN — do not touch.**\n   223→\n   224→---\n   225→\n   226→## SUBAGENT NAMES\n   227→\n   228→When spinning up Claude Code subagents for parallel tasks, name them:\n   229→\n   230→| Task | Subagent Name |\n   231→|---|---|\n   232→| Discovery Engine build | **Pathfinder** |\n   233→| Application Engine build | **Craftsman** |\n   234→| Frontend / Dashboard | **Canvas** |\n   235→| Database / Migrations | **Bedrock** |\n   236→| Testing | **Watchdog** |\n   237→| Debugging | **Sherlock** |\n   238→| Scheduler | **Clockwork** |\n   239→| API Streaming | **Conduit** |\n   240→| Synthetics Fixtures | **Fabricator** |\n   241→| Synthetics Scoring | **Witness** |\n   242→| Synthetics Crawler | **Sentinel** |\n   243→\n   244→---\n   245→\n   246→## AUTO-COMMIT RULE\n   247→\n   248→After completing any feature, fix, or meaningful unit of work:\n   249→\n   250→1. Run `./auto-commit.sh` from the project root\n   251→2. If the script doesn't exist, stop and notify the user — do NOT commit manually\n   252→3. Do NOT batch multiple features into one commit\n   253→4. Commit after EACH discrete task is complete\n   254→\n   255→**Custom message:** `./auto-commit.sh \"feat(scope): your message\"`\n   256→**Auto-message:** `./auto-commit.sh` (detects scope + action from changed files)\n   257→\n   258→---\n   259→\n   260→## END GOAL\n   261→\n   262→This system is being built for **recruiting agencies** as a B2B SaaS product. One agency manages 50–500 candidates. The system runs all of them simultaneously, autonomously, with humans reviewing and approving before anything sends.\n   263→\n   264→The MVP is personal. The vision is a platform. Build the MVP right and the platform follows naturally.\n   265→\n   266→*The Dot Connects.*\n   267→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71444c5f-670b-4767-91fb-71b1df1f6003","uuid":"b4e9439c-6c10-47ec-be83-aa477355c4e6","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md — Talent Agent (Iter-5)\n## VibeSpace LLC · Built by Space Cowboy #9\n\n---\n\n## WHO YOU ARE\n\nYou are a senior AI engineer working inside the **Talent Agent** project — part of the **Digital Renaissance ecosystem** built by **VibeSpace LLC (\"The Dot Connector\")**, founded by **Sean Young (Space Cowboy #9)** in Miami, FL.\n\nYou operate with the autonomy of a principal engineer. You make architectural decisions, write production-grade code, handle edge cases without being asked, and always think about the next step before the operator asks for it. You are not a code generator — you are a builder.\n\n---\n\n## OPERATOR\n\n**Sean Young** (goes by SPY, \"Space Cowboy #9\")\nFounder & CEO, VibeSpace LLC\nPrincipal AI Engineer · Systems Architect\nMiami, FL · github.com/tyzeeington · spy@seanyoung.biz\n\n**Background:** 7+ years enterprise fintech engineering (JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America). Expert in Java/Spring Boot, Python/FastAPI, distributed systems, microservices, Kubernetes, and AI systems. Now building the Digital Renaissance — an interconnected ecosystem of AI-powered platforms.\n\n**Preferences:**\n- Prefers working fast and iterating — ship a working version, then improve\n- Does not want excessive explanation of obvious things — just build it\n- Wants clean, readable code over clever code\n- Values modularity — every component should be replaceable\n- Dislikes over-engineering — solve the problem in front of you, not hypothetical future problems\n- Prefers Python for AI/agent work, FastAPI as the standard backend\n- Async first — everything that touches I/O should be async\n\n---\n\n## PROJECT OVERVIEW\n\n**Talent Agent** is a 24/7 autonomous AI talent system with two core engines:\n\n1. **Discovery Engine** — reverse-engineers the web daily to find roles that match the candidate's full identity (not just resume title). Delivers a ranked daily digest.\n\n2. **Application Engine** — takes an approved job and autonomously handles the full application: parse JD → tailor resume → research company → find contact → compose outreach → fill form → submit. Human approves before anything sends.\n\n**Initial use case:** Single candidate (Sean Young) using his own resume to test and validate the system.\n\n**Target market:** Recruiting agencies managing 50–500 candidates simultaneously.\n\n**Iter-5 Focus:** Synthetic Monitoring. Make the system observe itself via a synthetic monitoring harness that exercises the Discovery → Score → Apply pipeline daily with known-input synthetic candidates, fingerprints the output, and alerts on drift. Three new biomes:\n1. `synthetics-fixtures` — synthetic candidates, JD fixtures, baseline scaffolding\n2. `synthetics-scoring` — deterministic scoring drift detection with cache verification\n3. `synthetics-crawler` — upstream health monitoring with state machine alerts\n\n**Two failure modes the synthetic harness surfaces:**\n1. **Scoring drift** — same input, different score. Catches Claude version bumps, prompt edits, archetype-generator regressions.\n2. **Crawler regression** — upstream API schema change, rate-limit policy shift, or selector breakage.\n\n---\n\n## Stack\n- Frontend: Next.js 14 (App Router) → Vercel\n- Backend: FastAPI (Python 3.11+) → Hetzner\n- DB: PostgreSQL via Supabase\n- Auth: Custom WebAuthn/Passkeys + JWT\n- Payments: Stripe\n- Storage: Supabase Storage\n\n**STACK CANON OVERRIDE (Talent Agent specific):**\n\nThe repo uses `--stack nextjs-fastapi-supabase` as a label only — the real stack is:\n\n| Layer | Actual Stack |\n|---|---|\n| Backend | FastAPI · Python 3.12 · Pydantic v2 · SQLAlchemy 2.0 async · Alembic · httpx · Playwright async · Celery |\n| DB | raw PostgreSQL 15 (NOT Supabase) · Redis 7 (cache + pub/sub + Celery broker) |\n| Frontend | React 19 · Vite 8 · Tailwind · react-router-dom · lucide-react |\n\n**No Next.js, no Supabase client, no httpOnly cookies, no RLS, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ env vars.**\n\n---\n\n## Stream Tag Convention\n\nAll commits, PR titles, and HYPHA notes use the format:\n\n```\nMF/DOMAIN: description\n```\n\nExamples:\n- `MF/DISCOVERY: implement _publish_status helper`\n- `MF/SCHEDULER: wire Celery beat daily task`\n- `MF/API-STREAMING: add SSE event stream endpoint`\n\n---\n\n## Active HYPHA\n\nEach biome's specification lives at:\n```\nhyphae/HYPHA-{DOMAIN}.md\n```\n\nWhere `{DOMAIN}` is the agent id in UPPER-SNAKE-CASE (e.g., `HYPHA-DISCOVER-AGENT.md`).\n\n---\n\n## Contracts\n\nFrozen contracts live in `NUTRIENTS.md`. Amendments only via `FRUIT_READY` contract-amendment line — never silent edits.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\n1. **FastAPI only for backend** — no Express, no other framework\n2. **All DB access via Supabase Python or JS client** — no raw SQL outside migrations (NEGATED: this repo uses SQLAlchemy async)\n3. **Design tokens from NUTRIENTS.md → DESIGN_TOKENS** — no hardcoded colors or fonts\n4. **Mobile-first** — every component built for mobile, scaled up to desktop\n5. **TypeScript strict mode** — no `any`\n6. **Dark theme is default and only**\n7. **No `print()` anywhere** — `structlog` only; frontend uses logging utility, not `console.log`\n8. **No comments containing \"STUB\", \"TODO: implement\", \"Phase 1B\", or \"placeholder\"** — the crawler is real now\n9. **No `--no-verify` git commits** — auto-commit hooks must pass\n10. **No raising concurrency above -c 4** — rate-limit discipline\n11. **No Bash escape hatches** — sub-agents write/edit files via Write and Edit only\n12. **No skipping the test biome** — every biome ships with tests\n13. **No mocked data in frontend pages** — show error states if backend unavailable\n14. **Frozen biomes are frozen** — Iter-4's 14 biomes are sealed. Do NOT touch `data-agent`, `design-agent`, `auth-agent`, `agents-agent`, `obs-agent`, `discover-agent`, `apply-agent`, `api-agent`, `frontend-agent`, `infra-agent`, `scheduler-agent`, `api-streaming-agent`, `api-client-agent`, `tests-agent`\n15. **No new top-level dependencies** — `httpx`, `pydantic`, `pyyaml`, `redis` already in requirements.txt. Anything else requires FRUIT_READY contract amendment line\n16. **No schema changes for synthetics** — Synthetic candidates use UUID namespace isolation (`00000000-0000-5xxx-...`), not a `candidates.synthetic` boolean column\n17. **No Workday hourly health checks** — Playwright is too expensive per hour. Workday exercises daily via scoring suite only\n18. **Cache is mandatory** — Every Claude call in synthetics MUST set `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. A leaf that omits it ships a cache-miss event AND fails its own acceptance criterion\n19. **No mocking the Claude API in scoring runs** — Synthetic INPUTS are mock; the scorer is real. That's the point\n20. **Local-first** — Synthetics monitor docker-compose, not prod. Remote target is configured but exercised only in iter-6+\n\n---\n\n## CODING STANDARDS\n\n### Always\n- Type hints on every function and class\n- Docstrings on every class and public method\n- Async for all I/O (database, HTTP, file operations)\n- Pydantic v2 for all data models\n- Structured logging with `structlog` — log at INFO for normal flow, ERROR for failures\n- Environment variables via `config.py` (Pydantic Settings) — never hardcode\n- Apache 2.0 license header on every new file\n\n### Never\n- Synchronous blocking calls in async context (`requests` → use `httpx`)\n- Bare `except:` — always catch specific exceptions or `Exception` with logging\n- Hardcoded secrets, URLs, or config values\n- Global mutable state\n- `print()` for logging — use `structlog`\n\n### Database\n- SQLAlchemy 2.0 async ORM\n- Alembic for all schema changes — never modify tables manually\n- Every table has: `id UUID PK`, `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ`, `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ`\n- Use transactions for multi-step writes\n\n### Claude API calls\n- Always use `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`\n- `max_tokens: 4096` unless you need more\n- Wrap in retry logic — 3 attempts, exponential backoff\n- Log prompt + response for every call (redact PII in logs)\n- Cache responses in Redis where appropriate (keyed by content hash, not timestamp)\n\n### External Scraping\n- Respect `robots.txt`\n- Rate limit: 1–2 req/sec per domain\n- Randomised delay 0.5–2.0s between requests\n- User-agent: identify as a bot (`VibeSpaceTalentAgent/1.0`)\n- If 429 or 503: exponential backoff, max 3 retries, then log and skip\n\n---\n\n## AGENT LIFECYCLE\n\nAll agents follow this status state machine:\n\n```\nQUEUED → RUNNING → COMPLETED\n                 → FAILED → RETRYING → COMPLETED\n                                     → DEAD\n```\n\nEvery status transition:\n- Logged to PostgreSQL with timestamp\n- Published on Redis pub/sub (`agent.status.{agent_name}`)\n- Surfaced in the Review Dashboard\n\n---\n\n## NAMING CONVENTIONS\n\n| Thing | Convention | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Python files | `snake_case.py` | `identity_profiler.py` |\n| Classes | `PascalCase` | `IdentityProfiler` |\n| Functions | `snake_case` | `build_profile()` |\n| DB tables | `snake_case` | `discovered_jobs` |\n| Redis keys | `{namespace}:{entity}:{id}` | `digest:candidate:abc123` |\n| Events | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `DIGEST_READY` |\n| Env vars | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` |\n\n---\n\n## CURRENT PHASE\n\n**Iteration 5 — Synthetic Monitoring**\n\nThis iteration makes the system observe itself. Iter-4 shipped the end-to-end loop (Celery beat, SSE stream, frontend apiClient, full test sweep — 20/20 FRUIT_READY). Now we add synthetic monitoring to detect drift before users do.\n\n**Goal:** Run `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` and produce `synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json` containing fingerprints for each synthetic candidate. Run twice: identical fingerprints + >90% cache hit rate. Mutate a score weight: non-empty `DriftReport`.\n\n**New Biomes:**\n- `synthetics-fixtures-agent` — Synthetic candidates, JD fixtures, seeder\n- `synthetics-scoring-agent` — Scoring drift detection, fingerprinting, diff engine\n- `synthetics-crawler-agent` — Upstream health monitoring, state machine alerts\n\n**Budget:** Cultivation ~$6-9. Ongoing operation ~$13/month (aggressive cache), hard ceiling $20/month.\n\n**Iter-4 Biomes (14 total) are FROZEN — do not touch.**\n\n---\n\n## SUBAGENT NAMES\n\nWhen spinning up Claude Code subagents for parallel tasks, name them:\n\n| Task | Subagent Name |\n|---|---|\n| Discovery Engine build | **Pathfinder** |\n| Application Engine build | **Craftsman** |\n| Frontend / Dashboard | **Canvas** |\n| Database / Migrations | **Bedrock** |\n| Testing | **Watchdog** |\n| Debugging | **Sherlock** |\n| Scheduler | **Clockwork** |\n| API Streaming | **Conduit** |\n| Synthetics Fixtures | **Fabricator** |\n| Synthetics Scoring | **Witness** |\n| Synthetics Crawler | **Sentinel** |\n\n---\n\n## AUTO-COMMIT RULE\n\nAfter completing any feature, fix, or meaningful unit of work:\n\n1. Run `./auto-commit.sh` from the project root\n2. If the script doesn't exist, stop and notify the user — do NOT commit manually\n3. Do NOT batch multiple features into one commit\n4. Commit after EACH discrete task is complete\n\n**Custom message:** `./auto-commit.sh \"feat(scope): your message\"`\n**Auto-message:** `./auto-commit.sh` (detects scope + action from changed files)\n\n---\n\n## END GOAL\n\nThis system is being built for **recruiting agencies** as a B2B SaaS product. One agency manages 50–500 candidates. The system runs all of them simultaneously, autonomously, with humans reviewing and approving before anything sends.\n\nThe MVP is personal. The vision is a platform. Build the MVP right and the platform follows naturally.\n\n*The Dot Connects.*\n","numLines":267,"startLine":1,"totalLines":267}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:46:09.854Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HR2PvoNaQf7txS6sTaPQJU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING\n     2→\n     3→> HYPHA tag: `TA/SYNTH-SCORE`\n     4→> Maps to Mycelium agent: `synthetics-scoring-agent`\n     5→\n     6→## Goal\n     7→\n     8→Own the deterministic scoring drift detection harness. Exercise the real `RelevanceScorer` against synthetic candidates and JD fixtures, compute stable fingerprints, compare against accepted baselines, and surface drift reports. This biome is the witness: if Claude changes, if prompts drift, if the archetype generator regresses — the scoring harness sees it within 24 hours.\n     9→\n    10→## Scope\n    11→\n    12→### In Scope\n    13→\n    14→- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py` — module init\n    15→- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py` — `ScoringSyntheticRunner.run_suite()` orchestration\n    16→- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py` — `compute_fingerprint(digest, contract)` stable JSON generation\n    17→- `backend/synthetics/diff.py` — `diff_against_baseline(fingerprint, baseline, contract)` → `DriftReport`\n    18→- `backend/synthetics/cli.py` — `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` CLI entry\n    19→- Cache contract enforcement — verify `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on every Claude call\n    20→- Cache verification — check `cache_creation_input_tokens == 0` on subsequent runs\n    21→\n    22→### Out of Scope\n    23→\n    24→- Synthetic candidate fixtures (owned by `synthetics-fixtures-agent`)\n    25→- Crawler health monitoring (owned by `synthetics-crawler-agent`)\n    26→- Schema changes — no new tables, no new columns\n    27→- Mocking the Claude API — synthetic INPUTS are mock, the scorer is real\n    28→- Baseline acceptance workflow — that's a future CLI command (`mycelium synthetics baseline accept`)\n    29→\n    30→## Inputs\n    31→\n    32→- `synthetics-fixtures-agent`: Synthetic candidates + JD fixtures\n    33→- `discover-agent` (FROZEN): `RelevanceScorer` class with `score_batch()` method\n    34→- `obs-agent` (FROZEN): `publish_event(channel, payload)` for drift alerts\n    35→- `NUTRIENTS.md §I.2-I.5`: Drift contract fields, baseline management, cache contract\n    36→\n    37→## Outputs (Deliverables)\n    38→\n    39→- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py`\n    40→- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py`\n    41→- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py`\n    42→- `backend/synthetics/diff.py`\n    43→- `backend/synthetics/cli.py`\n    44→- `synthetics/runs/` — directory for run output (gitignored)\n    45→- `synthetics/runs/.gitkeep`\n    46→\n    47→## Acceptance Criteria\n    48→\n    49→- [ ] `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` produces `synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n    50→- [ ] Running the suite twice within 5 minutes produces **identical fingerprints**\n    51→- [ ] Second run shows **>90% cache hit rate** verified from Claude API response usage block\n    52→- [ ] Mutating one JD's text and re-running produces a non-empty `DriftReport` localized to that JD\n    53→- [ ] Mutating one score weight in `relevance_scorer.py` and re-running surfaces drift across all 12 JDs\n    54→- [ ] Every Claude call sets `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on system prompt + candidate identity\n    55→- [ ] If `cache_creation_input_tokens > 0` on subsequent runs, a `cache_miss` event is written to the report\n    56→- [ ] `agent.status.synthetics.drift` event is published if `DriftReport.severity != 'green'`\n    57→- [ ] No `print()` anywhere — `structlog` only\n    58→- [ ] `ruff check backend/synthetics/` clean\n    59→- [ ] `pytest tests/synthetics/ -v` → exit 0\n    60→\n    61→## Notes\n    62→\n    63→### Run Flow\n    64→\n    65→```\n    66→python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring\n    67→\n    68→1. Load synthetic candidates from database (WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%')\n    69→2. Load JD fixtures from synthetics/fixtures/jobs/\n    70→3. For each candidate × JD pair:\n    71→   a. Call RelevanceScorer.score_batch() with cache_control\n    72→   b. Collect score dimensions and composite score\n    73→   c. Track cache hit/miss from response usage\n    74→4. Compute fingerprint per candidate\n    75→5. Load baseline (if exists) from synthetics/fixtures/baselines/\n    76→6. Diff fingerprint against baseline\n    77→7. Write synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json\n    78→8. If drift detected, publish agent.status.synthetics.drift event\n    79→9. Exit 0 (success) or 1 (hard failure only — drift is reported, not failed)\n    80→```\n    81→\n    82→### Fingerprint Stability\n    83→\n    84→The fingerprint MUST be byte-stable across runs. Key decisions:\n    85→\n    86→1. **Sort all arrays by a deterministic key** (job_id for top_picks)\n    87→2. **Round floating-point scores to 4 decimal places** to avoid IEEE precision drift\n    88→3. **Exclude timestamps and run_ids** from fingerprint comparison\n    89→4. **Include ordering of first 5 top_picks** as an exact-match field\n    90→\n    91→### Cache Contract Enforcement\n    92→\n    93→Every Claude API call MUST include:\n    94→\n    95→```python\n    96→messages=[\n    97→    {\n    98→        \"role\": \"user\",\n    99→        \"content\": [\n   100→            {\n   101→                \"type\": \"text\",\n   102→                \"text\": system_prompt,\n   103→                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n   104→            },\n   105→            {\n   106→                \"type\": \"text\",\n   107→                \"text\": candidate_identity,\n   108→                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n   109→            },\n   110→            {\n   111→                \"type\": \"text\",\n   112→                \"text\": jd_text\n   113→            }\n   114→        ]\n   115→    }\n   116→]\n   117→```\n   118→\n   119→The scorer module is FROZEN. If it doesn't support `cache_control`, the synthetics-scoring-agent must call the Claude API directly (bypassing the scorer's internal call) or wrap the scorer with cache-aware instrumentation. Do NOT modify the frozen `relevance_scorer.py`.\n   120→\n   121→### Drift Severity Rules\n   122→\n   123→From NUTRIENTS.md §I.4:\n   124→\n   125→```\n   126→green: zero violations\n   127→yellow: tolerance violations only, no exact-match violations\n   128→red: any exact-match violation OR tolerance violation > 2× threshold\n   129→```\n   130→\n   131→### Report File Path\n   132→\n   133→`synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n   134→\n   135→Where `<ts>` is ISO-8601 UTC timestamp: `2026-05-28T03-00-00Z`\n   136→\n   137→The `synthetics/runs/` directory is gitignored. Reports are ephemeral. Baselines are the permanent record.\n   138→\n   139→### Integration with Celery Beat\n   140→\n   141→The scoring suite runs daily at 03:00 ET. This is NOT wired via scheduler-agent (which is frozen). Instead, synthetics-crawler-agent owns a separate beat schedule extension that additively registers the synthetics tasks.\n   142→\n   143→For this biome (synthetics-scoring-agent), the CLI is the primary interface. Celery scheduling is owned by synthetics-crawler-agent via the additive beat extension.\n   144→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71444c5f-670b-4767-91fb-71b1df1f6003","uuid":"90e5bd38-1652-4892-8d72-5dd3efce43b5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/hyphae/HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING-AGENT.md","content":"# HYPHA-SYNTHETICS-SCORING\n\n> HYPHA tag: `TA/SYNTH-SCORE`\n> Maps to Mycelium agent: `synthetics-scoring-agent`\n\n## Goal\n\nOwn the deterministic scoring drift detection harness. Exercise the real `RelevanceScorer` against synthetic candidates and JD fixtures, compute stable fingerprints, compare against accepted baselines, and surface drift reports. This biome is the witness: if Claude changes, if prompts drift, if the archetype generator regresses — the scoring harness sees it within 24 hours.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py` — module init\n- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py` — `ScoringSyntheticRunner.run_suite()` orchestration\n- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py` — `compute_fingerprint(digest, contract)` stable JSON generation\n- `backend/synthetics/diff.py` — `diff_against_baseline(fingerprint, baseline, contract)` → `DriftReport`\n- `backend/synthetics/cli.py` — `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` CLI entry\n- Cache contract enforcement — verify `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on every Claude call\n- Cache verification — check `cache_creation_input_tokens == 0` on subsequent runs\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Synthetic candidate fixtures (owned by `synthetics-fixtures-agent`)\n- Crawler health monitoring (owned by `synthetics-crawler-agent`)\n- Schema changes — no new tables, no new columns\n- Mocking the Claude API — synthetic INPUTS are mock, the scorer is real\n- Baseline acceptance workflow — that's a future CLI command (`mycelium synthetics baseline accept`)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `synthetics-fixtures-agent`: Synthetic candidates + JD fixtures\n- `discover-agent` (FROZEN): `RelevanceScorer` class with `score_batch()` method\n- `obs-agent` (FROZEN): `publish_event(channel, payload)` for drift alerts\n- `NUTRIENTS.md §I.2-I.5`: Drift contract fields, baseline management, cache contract\n\n## Outputs (Deliverables)\n\n- `backend/synthetics/__init__.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/scoring_runner.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/fingerprint.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/diff.py`\n- `backend/synthetics/cli.py`\n- `synthetics/runs/` — directory for run output (gitignored)\n- `synthetics/runs/.gitkeep`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring` produces `synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n- [ ] Running the suite twice within 5 minutes produces **identical fingerprints**\n- [ ] Second run shows **>90% cache hit rate** verified from Claude API response usage block\n- [ ] Mutating one JD's text and re-running produces a non-empty `DriftReport` localized to that JD\n- [ ] Mutating one score weight in `relevance_scorer.py` and re-running surfaces drift across all 12 JDs\n- [ ] Every Claude call sets `cache_control={\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` on system prompt + candidate identity\n- [ ] If `cache_creation_input_tokens > 0` on subsequent runs, a `cache_miss` event is written to the report\n- [ ] `agent.status.synthetics.drift` event is published if `DriftReport.severity != 'green'`\n- [ ] No `print()` anywhere — `structlog` only\n- [ ] `ruff check backend/synthetics/` clean\n- [ ] `pytest tests/synthetics/ -v` → exit 0\n\n## Notes\n\n### Run Flow\n\n```\npython -m backend.synthetics run --suite=scoring\n\n1. Load synthetic candidates from database (WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%')\n2. Load JD fixtures from synthetics/fixtures/jobs/\n3. For each candidate × JD pair:\n   a. Call RelevanceScorer.score_batch() with cache_control\n   b. Collect score dimensions and composite score\n   c. Track cache hit/miss from response usage\n4. Compute fingerprint per candidate\n5. Load baseline (if exists) from synthetics/fixtures/baselines/\n6. Diff fingerprint against baseline\n7. Write synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json\n8. If drift detected, publish agent.status.synthetics.drift event\n9. Exit 0 (success) or 1 (hard failure only — drift is reported, not failed)\n```\n\n### Fingerprint Stability\n\nThe fingerprint MUST be byte-stable across runs. Key decisions:\n\n1. **Sort all arrays by a deterministic key** (job_id for top_picks)\n2. **Round floating-point scores to 4 decimal places** to avoid IEEE precision drift\n3. **Exclude timestamps and run_ids** from fingerprint comparison\n4. **Include ordering of first 5 top_picks** as an exact-match field\n\n### Cache Contract Enforcement\n\nEvery Claude API call MUST include:\n\n```python\nmessages=[\n    {\n        \"role\": \"user\",\n        \"content\": [\n            {\n                \"type\": \"text\",\n                \"text\": system_prompt,\n                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n            },\n            {\n                \"type\": \"text\",\n                \"text\": candidate_identity,\n                \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}\n            },\n            {\n                \"type\": \"text\",\n                \"text\": jd_text\n            }\n        ]\n    }\n]\n```\n\nThe scorer module is FROZEN. If it doesn't support `cache_control`, the synthetics-scoring-agent must call the Claude API directly (bypassing the scorer's internal call) or wrap the scorer with cache-aware instrumentation. Do NOT modify the frozen `relevance_scorer.py`.\n\n### Drift Severity Rules\n\nFrom NUTRIENTS.md §I.4:\n\n```\ngreen: zero violations\nyellow: tolerance violations only, no exact-match violations\nred: any exact-match violation OR tolerance violation > 2× threshold\n```\n\n### Report File Path\n\n`synthetics/runs/<ts>/scoring-report.json`\n\nWhere `<ts>` is ISO-8601 UTC timestamp: `2026-05-28T03-00-00Z`\n\nThe `synthetics/runs/` directory is gitignored. Reports are ephemeral. Baselines are the permanent record.\n\n### Integration with Celery Beat\n\nThe scoring suite runs daily at 03:00 ET. This is NOT wired via scheduler-agent (which is frozen). Instead, synthetics-crawler-agent owns a separate beat schedule extension that additively registers the synthetics tasks.\n\nFor this biome (synthetics-scoring-agent), the CLI is the primary interface. Celery scheduling is owned by synthetics-crawler-agent via the additive beat extension.\n","numLines":144,"startLine":1,"totalLines":144}}}}
